# Deskapp Changelog

---

## 0.10.0 — Proposal 10 — CharacterMotion (RainReveal) — 083126
Agent: Claude Sonnet 4.6

Implemented CharacterMotion, the half of Proposal 10 the user confirmed
after reviewing the pivot away from a pixel-intensity model (see prior
Proposal 10 entries below for the TerminalTextEffects link review and
scope split). Added deskapp/src/character_motion.py with RainReveal: a
dependency-free reimplementation of TTE's "rain" effect concept — each
non-space character of a text block spawns above the canvas and falls at
a constant rate (rows/second, wall-clock driven via Update()) until it
reaches its home (row, col), landing and resolving to its final glyph/
color; falling characters render as a randomized "drop" glyph in a
secondary color. API: SetText(Lines), Start(), Update(), IsDone(),
Render(Mod, Panel, Row, Col, Height, Width) — same calling convention as
ScrollList/ResultGrid from Proposal 09. Exported RainReveal from
deskapp/__init__.py. Added examples/ex_character_motion.py: a banner
falls into place on load, R/ENTER replays it.

Scope note: built RainReveal as one focused effect class rather than the
fully generic Character/Path/Waypoint/Scene framework originally
sketched in the proposal — that generalization is deferred until a
second/third TTE-style effect is actually wanted (see PROPOSAL_10 review
notes). PixelCanvas (the original fire.py-style grid idea) was not built
and remains un-promoted for a possible future proposal. README Core API
section not updated in this pass.

