## Proposal 10 (drafted, not yet implemented) — PixelCanvasEffect — 083126
Agent: Claude Sonnet 4.6

Promoted .github/proposals/TODO_PixelCanvasEffect_083126.prop to
.github/proposals/PROPOSAL_10_PixelCanvasEffect_083126.prop at the user's
request, with checkboxes added. Proposal generalizes the "pixel space"
buffer/glyph-ramp pattern already present in deskapp/mods/fire.py's Flames
class into a shared PixelCanvas abstraction (deskapp/src/pixel_canvas.py),
refactors fire.py onto it, and adds a second effect module plus an
examples/ demo. Note: .gitignore excludes /.github/proposals/*, so the
.prop file itself is not tracked in git — this changelog entry is the
durable cross-session record; the .prop file must be regenerated or
force-added (git add -f) if it needs to persist. Version not yet rolled —
no code changed, awaiting user review of the proposal per the pipeline
(execution starts only once the user confirms the plan).

Update 083126: user supplied the reference link,
github.com/ChrisBuilds/terminaltexteffects (TTE). Reviewed TTE's README —
it is a character-animation engine (per-character home coordinate, Paths/
Waypoints for movement, Scenes for symbol/color keyframes over time),
not a pixel-intensity grid like fire.py. Revised PROPOSAL_10 to split the
work into two independent pieces: PixelCanvas (the original fire.py-style
idea) and a new CharacterMotion abstraction modeled on TTE's Path/Scene
concept, applied at a scope appropriate for a dependency-free TUI
framework (no bezier/easing library, deferred to a later proposal).
Awaiting user decision on which piece(s) to build before implementation.

